# What opens where (K2), on the notes `cursor.seed.ts` writes. The tree's cursor is put on the beds and the reader
# its select wire names shows them; the row opened hands the keys to that reader. A second reader is split off and
# pinned (the lock on its title), the links tile is held on the note it lists (its title says "held" and what on,
# while the reader moves on), and the tree's opens are wired to the pinned reader, so the next row opened lands
# beside it: the notice says where it landed, why, and the way back. Each title says where its tile's opens land,
# a press on that picks another tile on screen, the tile a note just landed in is marked, and the row under the
# tiles says where the keys of the tile that has them land.
tile.focus tile=tree
list.select n=-3
list.pick
tile.split tile=reader
reader.pin on=true tile=reader2
tile.hold on=true tile=backlinks
tile.link to=reader2 verb=open tile=tree
tile.focus tile=tree
tree.fold open=true
list.step by=1
list.pick
tile.focus tile=tree
